  "Question": "A house and store were sold for \\(\\$12000\\) each. The house was sold at a loss of \\(20\\%\\) of the cost, and the store at a gain of \\(20\\%\\) of the cost. The entire transaction resulted in:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "No loss or gain",
    "B": "Loss of \\(\\$1000\\)",
    "C": "Gain of \\(\\$1000\\)",
    "D": "Gain of \\(\\$2000\\)",
    "E": "None of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Each percentage is based on the property's original cost, so first recover those costs. The house sold for \\(80\\%\\) of its cost, while the store sold for \\(120\\%\\) of its cost. Thus, in dollars,\n\\[\n\\text{House cost}=\\frac{12000}{0.80}=15000,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Store cost}=\\frac{12000}{1.20}=10000.\n\\]\nThe total cost was \\(15000+10000=25000\\), and the total received was \\(12000+12000=24000\\). Therefore the transaction produced a loss of \\(25000-24000=1000\\) dollars, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
